1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,481
Your best friend's wedding is on Saturday, and you're giving a two-
minute toast.

2
00:00:04,641 --> 00:00:10,037
You'll be holding a glass and a microphone, and you want your eyes on
the couple, not on note cards.

3
00:00:10,197 --> 00:00:12,112
So the talk has to live in your head.

4
00:00:13,172 --> 00:00:19,742
Memory champions don't repeat lists. They walk through a place they
know and leave a vivid image at each spot.

5
00:00:19,902 --> 00:00:26,918
In a 2017 study in Neuron, six weeks of this method more than doubled
ordinary people's recall.

6
00:00:27,078 --> 00:00:30,832
Walk Your Talk brings that trick into your actual room, on SPECS.

7
00:00:31,892 --> 00:00:38,996
Pinch the glowing spot, and the first beat, thank everyone for coming,
becomes a sunflower bouquet on the kitchen island.

8
00:00:39,156 --> 00:00:47,304
The camping trip becomes a tent, the bowling alley a giant pin,
patience a golden snail, and the toast itself a champagne flute.

9
00:00:47,464 --> 00:00:50,335
A gold route joins them in the order you'll speak.

10
00:00:51,395 --> 00:00:52,710
Now walk the route.

11
00:00:52,870 --> 00:00:58,502
As you reach each object, it wakes up and shows its beat, just long
enough to say it out loud.

12
00:00:58,662 --> 00:01:03,132
If the next spot is out of view, a small arrow and a soft chime point
the way.

13
00:01:03,292 --> 00:01:06,268
Can't walk the room? Pinch the next spot instead.

14
00:01:07,328 --> 00:01:08,803
Then the objects hide.

15
00:01:08,963 --> 00:01:13,933
Walk the route again, say each beat from memory, and pinch the
question mark to check.

16
00:01:14,093 --> 00:01:18,012
Got it, or missed: two big targets, right next to the object.

17
00:01:19,072 --> 00:01:20,994
Here, four of five came back.

18
00:01:21,154 --> 00:01:25,922
The debrief names the one that slipped, and builds a practice route
with only that beat.

19
00:01:26,082 --> 00:01:28,408
One more walk, and every beat is back.

20
00:01:29,468 --> 00:01:35,856
I planned it with the Devpost Learn plan-lens skill, and built it with
CLAD through the Lens Studio MCP.

21
00:01:36,016 --> 00:01:42,117
The five objects come from Lens Studio's 3D generator, and the sounds
from CLAD's synthesizer.

22
00:01:42,277 --> 00:01:48,218
Ten logic tests and seven LEAF scenarios pass in the preview, covering
every done criterion.

23
00:01:49,278 --> 00:01:55,592
This demo runs in Lens Studio's preview, in a simulated room, with
spots placed on its furniture.

24
00:01:55,752 --> 00:01:57,832
On glasses, you'd pinch your own.

25
00:01:57,992 --> 00:02:02,310
Next, type or say your own talk, and keep your palace between
rehearsals.

26
00:02:02,470 --> 00:02:06,022
Walk your talk, and keep your eyes on the people you're talking to.
